            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0268" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg256"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851D.001/10a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wiley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-20T00:00:00-04:00">March 20,
                            1943—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>511. For Murphy.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d225-f1"/> With respect to the situation
                    in French Guiana the French Military Mission here has informed Giraud of the
                    urgent necessity of sending a Governor to Cayenne. Colonel LeBel, from the
                    Military Mission here, left last night and arrives Cayenne Sunday <pb
                        facs="0269" n="257" xml:id="pg257"/> for the purpose of making contact with
                    local officials pending arrival of properly designated representative from
                    Giraud. Attempts are being made to have officials from other than North African
                    authorities proceed to French Guiana and UP despatch from London states deGaulle
                    has “appointed a Governor of the Colony”. Hope you will appreciate the necessity
                    of expediting the sending of Giraud’s representative with authority to assume
                    control in order that public order may be maintained and avoid any internal
                    disturbance or disorder.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d225-f1" n="38" xml:id="d225-f1-content">
                <p>Robert D. Murphy, United States Political Adviser, Staff of Supreme Allied
                    Commander, Mediterranean Theater, and Personal Representative of the President
                    in North Africa.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
